  "releaseNotes": "NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.RootstockOASIS v2.0.5\n\nConnects the OASIS to Rootstock (RSK) -- an EVM-compatible smart contract platform merge-mined with Bitcoin, inheriting Bitcoin's hash power while enabling Solidity contracts and DeFi. Stores OASIS holons, avatars, and rBTC-backed tokens. Part of the OASIS HOT-Swappable Provider Architecture. Ecosystem: https://oasisomniverse.one\n\nWhat's new since v2.0.4\n- Fix Rootstock V2 query authority and configured chain factory ownership (a69578d)\n- MOVING DOCS AROUND (32a8004)\n- security: remove a committed testnet chain private key (and a block-explorer API key) from provider DNA files, test harness configs and .env; the Arbitrum test harness reads OASIS_TEST_CHAIN_PRIVATE_KEY instead. The key is still in git history: rotate it. (fefa98c)\n\nFull changelog\nhttps://github.com/NextGenSoftwareUK/OASIS/commits/master/Providers/Blockchain/NextGenSoftware.OASIS.API.Providers.RootstockOASIS",
